From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 06:19:22 -0700
Subject: [net] Stop PAC script auto-auth fetches in ProxyResolverWinHttp

Removes the retry with `fAutoLogonIfChallenged = TRUE` in
ProxyResolverWinHttp upon receiving ERROR_WINHTTP_LOGIN_FAILURE.

The auto-logon fallback was legacy behavior for older Windows versions
that has since been deprecated. Removing this retry aligns
ProxyResolverWinHttp with modern Windows guidance (MS16-077) as well as
the behavior of PacFileFetcherImpl and WindowsSystemProxyResolverImpl,
neither of which attempts automatic logon when retrieving PAC scripts.

Also adds unit tests verifying that an authentication challenge during
PAC retrieval fails without retrying with auto-logon.

Fixed: 533493992
Change-Id: I02be9263faded7790d38e3403af6e7425c3e351a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8288770
Commit-Queue: Sebastien Lalancette <seblalancette@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kenichi Ishibashi <bashi@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1690651}

